{"agent":"bgw","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The regression still monkeypatches `ddflow.services.changes.changed_paths` (`CH.changed_paths`) and counts only that name. The bug and the scan path under test are `CM.verdict` / `ddflow/services/completion/_changed.py`'s `changed_paths`, which recovery now calls with a shared `cache` (`L.scan` → `_note_landed` → `CM.verdict(..., cache=cache)`). A function already bound by `from ddflow.services.changes import changed_paths` is not replaced by `setattr(CH, \"changed_paths\", counting)`, so with T1–T3 merged and lapsed an unfixed verdict can still re-diff each item on every probe while `derived` stays empty. `len(derived) == len(items)` then fails on both the unfixed and the fixed code (false red), or never sees the ~5 git derivations per item if those calls never go through the patched attribute. The bound change only stops a vacuous `<=` pass; it does not wrap the hot path.","digest":"10f120cb2a2eccaa","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_recover_scan_cache.py:66","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_recover_scan_cache.py:66"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":14173,"diff_sha":"b879149b77c279a088dd2e86788b68e370c7108aaa02cfbc25c73851d589372a","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-Bc52bf2ef41","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":0.8,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"d991d24906b6f24d","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bc52bf2ef41.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261109T134016Z-3edefaac.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"e3f2d550e07c30de1d6fa1dd8aebab99a718b75e","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/completion/_changed.py":"100644 bfe2ffc5dcc051c444d9ca7ae5e9910143801718","ddflow/services/completion/rules.p